    "question": {
      ":question/id": "ccdc6336-3e2c-5cdd-af8a-b0663513cbfd",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/repairs/2026-10-19-checkbox-nonempty/patched-samples/17592186054676/assets/a4d495b0df3cb2ca1227ad4832aaa1023bc5f44bd4eff603cfcc6e2f8f5e237f.png)\n\nWhich of the given points lie on the line $y=-3x$?",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The plotted points correspond to the $xy$-pairs $A(-3,9)$, $B(1,0)$, $C(0,0)$.\n\nTo check whether a point lies on the line, we substitute the coordinates of the point into the equation and determine whether the resulting statement is true.\n\n- Substituting the point $A(-3,9)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= -3x \\\\ (9) &= -3(-3) \\\\ 9 &= 9 && \\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $A$ does lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $B(1,0)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= -3x \\\\ (0) &= -3(1) \\\\ 0 &= -3 && \\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $B$ does not lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $C(0,0)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= -3x \\\\ (0) &= -3(0) \\\\ 0 &= 0 && \\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $C$ does lie on the line.\n\nFinally, only points $A$ and $C$ lie on the line.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "1357195a-22ca-531c-8d38-d001231e09aa",
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
