      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/repairs/2026-10-19-checkbox-nonempty/patched-samples/17592186054676/assets/e0c895dd3e919f4f89721ce214a16ce7027249f9230ecddb7d1f7346628452b7.png)\n\nWhich of the given points lie on the line $y=-2x+1$?",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The plotted points correspond to the $xy$-pairs $A(1,0)$, $B(0,0)$, $C(-3,7)$.\n\nTo check whether a point lies on the line, we substitute the coordinates of the point into the equation and determine whether the resulting statement is true.\n\n- Substituting the point $A(1,0)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= -2x+1 \\\\ (0) &= -2(1)+1 \\\\ 0 &= -1 && \\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $A$ does not lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $B(0,0)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= -2x+1 \\\\ (0) &= -2(0)+1 \\\\ 0 &= 1 && \\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $B$ does not lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $C(-3,7)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= -2x+1 \\\\ (7) &= -2(-3)+1 \\\\ 7 &= 7 && \\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $C$ does lie on the line.\n\nFinally, only point $C$ lies on the line.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "430a0a2b-d27f-5385-a96a-17b6b8b08318",
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
