      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/repairs/2026-10-19-checkbox-nonempty/patched-samples/17592186054676/assets/e914b900cb73411b47ca8761b94b0edae83406b2d75dd2286d90d11c94c0c730.png)\n\nWhich of the given points lie on the line $y=-2x+3$?",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The plotted points correspond to the $xy$-pairs $A(-2,7)$, $B(1,1)$, $C(0,5)$.\n\nTo check whether a point lies on the line, we substitute the coordinates of the point into the equation and determine whether the resulting statement is true.\n\n- Substituting the point $A(-2,7)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= -2x+3 \\\\ (7) &= -2(-2)+3 \\\\ 7 &= 7 && \\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $A$ does lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $B(1,1)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= -2x+3 \\\\ (1) &= -2(1)+3 \\\\ 1 &= 1 && \\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $B$ does lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $C(0,5)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= -2x+3 \\\\ (5) &= -2(0)+3 \\\\ 5 &= 3 && \\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $C$ does not lie on the line.\n\nFinally, only points $A$ and $B$ lie on the line.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "0373dbae-cbce-5b41-a32a-6603e5eaee5b",
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
