      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/repairs/2026-10-19-checkbox-nonempty/patched-samples/17592186054676/assets/714c4d8f323d7834f963e8be2f5dfc28badac1a5685a26e2351fa85a9d90ff01.png)\n\nWhich of the given points lie on the line $y=-2x-2$?",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The plotted points correspond to the $xy$-pairs $A(-1,0)$, $B(1,-7)$, $C(-4,7)$.\n\nTo check whether a point lies on the line, we substitute the coordinates of the point into the equation and determine whether the resulting statement is true.\n\n- Substituting the point $A(-1,0)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= -2x-2 \\\\ (0) &= -2(-1)-2 \\\\ 0 &= 0 && \\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $A$ does lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $B(1,-7)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= -2x-2 \\\\ (-7) &= -2(1)-2 \\\\ -7 &= -4 && \\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $B$ does not lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $C(-4,7)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= -2x-2 \\\\ (7) &= -2(-4)-2 \\\\ 7 &= 6 && \\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $C$ does not lie on the line.\n\nFinally, only point $A$ lies on the line.",
