      ":question/worked-solution": "The plotted points correspond to the $xy$-pairs $A(-2,-2)$, $B(1,-6)$, $C(-3,0)$.\n\nTo check whether a point lies on the line, we substitute the coordinates of the point into the equation and determine whether the resulting statement is true.\n\n- Substituting the point $A(-2,-2)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= -2x-4 \\\\ (-2) &= -2(-2)-4 \\\\ -2 &= 0 && \\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $A$ does not lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $B(1,-6)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= -2x-4 \\\\ (-6) &= -2(1)-4 \\\\ -6 &= -6 && \\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $B$ does lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $C(-3,0)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= -2x-4 \\\\ (0) &= -2(-3)-4 \\\\ 0 &= 2 && \\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $C$ does not lie on the line.\n\nFinally, only point $B$ lies on the line.",
