    "question": {
      ":question/id": "4a812412-4fad-5635-ba0e-8c85ec04d059",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/repairs/2026-10-19-checkbox-nonempty/patched-samples/17592186054676/assets/33254f5d83b70653139043f822c77f22d5cb573b602d49372d5b915005439e1d.png)\n\nWhich of the given points lie on the line $y=-2x-1$?",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The plotted points correspond to the $xy$-pairs $A(-4,7)$, $B(2,-8)$, $C(-2,4)$.\n\nTo check whether a point lies on the line, we substitute the coordinates of the point into the equation and determine whether the resulting statement is true.\n\n- Substituting the point $A(-4,7)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= -2x-1 \\\\ (7) &= -2(-4)-1 \\\\ 7 &= 7 && \\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $A$ does lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $B(2,-8)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= -2x-1 \\\\ (-8) &= -2(2)-1 \\\\ -8 &= -5 && \\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $B$ does not lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $C(-2,4)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= -2x-1 \\\\ (4) &= -2(-2)-1 \\\\ 4 &= 3 && \\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $C$ does not lie on the line.\n\nFinally, only point $A$ lies on the line.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
