      ":question/worked-solution": "The plotted points correspond to the $xy$-pairs $A(0,-1)$, $B(2,-5)$, $C(-2,5)$.\n\nTo check whether a point lies on the line, we substitute the coordinates of the point into the equation and determine whether the resulting statement is true.\n\n- Substituting the point $A(0,-1)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= -3x-1 \\\\ (-1) &= -3(0)-1 \\\\ -1 &= -1 && \\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $A$ does lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $B(2,-5)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= -3x-1 \\\\ (-5) &= -3(2)-1 \\\\ -5 &= -7 && \\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $B$ does not lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $C(-2,5)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= -3x-1 \\\\ (5) &= -3(-2)-1 \\\\ 5 &= 5 && \\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $C$ does lie on the line.\n\nFinally, only points $A$ and $C$ lie on the line.",
