      ":question/worked-solution": "The plotted points correspond to the $xy$-pairs $A(0,6)$, $B(1,4)$, $C(3,-2)$.\n\nTo check whether a point lies on the line, we substitute the coordinates of the point into the equation and determine whether the resulting statement is true.\n\n- Substituting the point $A(0,6)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= -2x+6 \\\\ (6) &= -2(0)+6 \\\\ 6 &= 6 && \\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $A$ does lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $B(1,4)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= -2x+6 \\\\ (4) &= -2(1)+6 \\\\ 4 &= 4 && \\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $B$ does lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $C(3,-2)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= -2x+6 \\\\ (-2) &= -2(3)+6 \\\\ -2 &= 0 && \\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $C$ does not lie on the line.\n\nFinally, only points $A$ and $B$ lie on the line.",
