      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/repairs/2026-10-19-checkbox-nonempty/patched-samples/17592186054676/assets/0c653181f933f8d30a20de5699f1b8e02f4d8c7133001cfcb99d5f5daa64c894.png)\n\nWhich of the given points lie on the line $y=-2x-1$?",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The plotted points correspond to the $xy$-pairs $A(0,-1)$, $B(-1,0)$, $C(-3,4)$.\n\nTo check whether a point lies on the line, we substitute the coordinates of the point into the equation and determine whether the resulting statement is true.\n\n- Substituting the point $A(0,-1)$ results in a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= -2x-1 \\\\ (-1) &= -2(0)-1 \\\\ -1 &= -1 && \\checkmark\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $A$ does lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $B(-1,0)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= -2x-1 \\\\ (0) &= -2(-1)-1 \\\\ 0 &= 1 && \\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $B$ does not lie on the line.\n\n- Substituting the point $C(-3,4)$ results in a false statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y &= -2x-1 \\\\ (4) &= -2(-3)-1 \\\\ 4 &= 5 && \\times\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the point $C$ does not lie on the line.\n\nFinally, only point $A$ lies on the line.",
